  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: deciding whether a die is biased</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: Find an expected frequency and use it to decide which of two dice is more likely to be biased, with a reason.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section C, question C4 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: two dice instead of spinners, randomised curated data, with a conclusion and a reason to choose.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
